@startuml
title Mandate Lens - detailed class and request flow
!pragma layout smetana
left to right direction
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam linetype ortho

class Merchant <<external caller>>
class GuardService <<external AgentGuard service>>
class DB <<PostgreSQL trust schema>>

package "AgentPulse - write/check flow" as PulseWrite {
  class MerchantOperationController <<REST entry point>> {
    +check(request)
    +reportResult(operationId, result)
  }
  class MerchantOperationService <<request coordinator>> {
    +check(request)
    +result(operationId, result)
    -validate(request)
    -coordinateGuardAndPersistence()
  }
  class MandateService <<mandate lookup>> {
    +findByJourneyId(journeyId)
  }
  class Mandate <<authorization facts>> {
    mandateId
    journeyId
    merchantId
    maxAmount
    allowedCategories
    expiresAt
  }
  class PendingOperationRepository <<operation storage>> {
    +findByIdempotencyKey(merchantId, key)
    +create(operation, cart, action)
    +saveDecision(operationId, decision)
    +saveCallback(eventId, result)
  }
  class GuardDecisionRecorder <<save decision and event>> {
    +record(operation, decision, reasons, rules)
  }
  class EventStore <<journey event storage>> {
    +save(event)
    +findByJourneyId(journeyId)
  }
  class OperationExpiryScheduler <<background timer>> {
    +expireOverdueOperations()
    +expireInactiveJourneys()
  }
}

package "AgentGuard - connection code in Mandate Lens" as GuardAdapter {
  interface AgentGuardClient {
    +evaluateCart(request)
    +evaluateCheckout(request)
  }
  class HttpAgentGuardClient <<HTTP adapter>> {
    +evaluateCart(request)
    +evaluateCheckout(request)
  }
  class EvaluateCartRequest <<whole cart to check>>
  class EvaluateCheckoutRequest <<final cart to check>>
  class GuardDecisionResponse <<decision facts>> {
    decisionId
    decision: GuardDecision
    reasons
    ruleResults
  }
}

package "AgentPulse - journey read flow" as PulseRead {
  class MerchantJourneyController <<REST read entry point>> {
    +getJourney(journeyId, merchantId)
  }
  class JourneyQueryService <<read coordinator>> {
    +getJourney(journeyId, merchantId)
    -checkMerchantOwnership(journeyId, merchantId)
    -assembleStoredFacts()
  }
  class JourneyReadRepository <<read-only database access>> {
    +findJourney(journeyId, merchantId)
    +findOperations(journeyId)
    +findDecisions(journeyId)
    +findEvents(journeyId)
  }
  class JourneyDetail <<returned journey view>> {
    journeyId
    merchantId
    cartId
    status
    latestEventType
    latestOutcome
    operations
    decisions
    ruleResults
    timeline
  }
}

Merchant --> MerchantOperationController : 1. send whole-cart check\n2. send actual result callback
MerchantOperationController --> MerchantOperationService : pass validated request
MerchantOperationService --> MandateService : find mandate for journey
MandateService --> Mandate : return limits and merchant link
MerchantOperationService --> PendingOperationRepository : 1. save pending operation\n2. update operation result
MerchantOperationService --> AgentGuardClient : evaluate proposed cart
AgentGuardClient <|.. HttpAgentGuardClient
HttpAgentGuardClient --> GuardService : send mandate and cart facts
GuardService --> GuardDecisionResponse : return ALLOW/BLOCK\nwith reasons and rule results
MerchantOperationService --> GuardDecisionRecorder : save Guard answer
GuardDecisionRecorder --> PendingOperationRepository : attach decision and status
GuardDecisionRecorder --> EventStore : add Guard check event
MerchantOperationService --> EventStore : add merchant result event\n(cart/payment success or failure)

Merchant --> MerchantJourneyController : 3. request saved journey after result/failure
MerchantJourneyController --> JourneyQueryService : ask for journey facts
JourneyQueryService --> JourneyReadRepository : find matching merchant and journey
JourneyReadRepository --> DB : read journey, operations, decisions, events
JourneyQueryService --> JourneyDetail : combine facts in time order
JourneyDetail --> MerchantJourneyController : response with reason facts
MerchantJourneyController --> Merchant : return journey details

OperationExpiryScheduler --> PendingOperationRepository : find operations with no callback
OperationExpiryScheduler --> EventStore : record timeout/expiry event

PendingOperationRepository --> DB : save/check operation state
GuardDecisionRecorder --> DB : save Guard decision and reasons
EventStore --> DB : append timeline event
JourneyReadRepository --> DB : read-only journey query

note bottom of PulseWrite
Check flow: Merchant -> Pulse -> Guard -> save decision/event -> Merchant.
After trying the change, Merchant sends a callback; Pulse saves the real outcome.
ALLOW means the merchant may try; it does not guarantee the cart change succeeded.
Routes: POST /api/v1/merchant-operations/check and
POST /api/v1/merchant-operations/{operationId}/result.
end note

note bottom of PulseRead
The read API returns stored facts. It does not re-run Guard or PayPal.
merchantId matching is only a local demo ownership check, not authentication.
Route: GET /api/v1/journeys/{journeyId}?merchantId={merchantId}.
end note

note bottom of GuardAdapter
These client and request/response classes live in Mandate Lens.
The policy rules and decision-making service belong to the AgentGuard teammate.
end note
@enduml
